Vote: REQUEST_CHANGES

- `PrintFarmer/Models/PrinterBackendCapabilities.swift:17-28` makes every capability a required `Bool`. If the backend omits one key, decode throws instead of defaulting that missing capability to `false`.
- `PrintFarmer/Services/PrinterService.swift:103-112` then catches that decoding failure and falls back to the static backend table, which can turn omitted capabilities back on instead of preserving the safe-by-default contract.
- `PrintFarmerTests/Models/PrinterBackendCapabilitiesTests.swift:13-205` covers full/partial/resin fixtures but never exercises an omitted-key payload, so this regression path is unprotected.

