Addressed all three blocking issues from Bishop's review:

- **Issue 1 — Safe-by-default Bool decoding**: Added CodingKeys enum and custom init(from decoder:) to PrinterBackendCapabilities. All 12 capability booleans now use decodeIfPresent(_:forKey:) ?? false. The three identity fields (printerId, printerName, backend) remain required and still throw on absence. A backend omitting any capability key will never cause a decode error — the field simply reads false.

- **Issue 2 — Fallback contract documented**: The fallback(for:) static method is preserved — still needed for total network failures (404s, network errors, completely malformed JSON). Updated its doc-comment with the new contract: it must not be used to infer capabilities from a partial server payload, because partial payloads now decode cleanly through the custom init.

- **Issue 3 — Omitted-key tests added**: Added two new XCTest cases in PrinterBackendCapabilitiesTests: testOmittedTemperatureControlDefaultsFalse (single omission — supportsTemperatureControl absent, asserts false on raw field and derived supportsBedTemperature) and testOmittedTemperatureAndMovementDefaultFalse (multiple omissions — only 4 keys present, asserts both omitted caps are false and explicit caps decode correctly).

Stack: PRs #4 and #7 have been rebased onto the new head of this branch with --force-with-lease.
